/*----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 CDISC SAS Macro Module: gen_tp_join_adsl.sas
 CDISC Algorithm Reference: 
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose: 
	Utility to create TRTA TRTP TRTAN TRTPN APERIOD APERIODC APHASE APERSDT APEREDT 
        APERSTM APERETM APERSDTM APEREDTM APERDY APERSDY and APEREDY variables. 

Assumptions: 
	Treatment related variables exist in the input dataset.
        If Time is being considered, both treatment time and analysis time 
          should be present in the input dataset.
        
Calls to: 
        %util_num_periods

Inputs: 
        Dataset after merge with ADSL.
            
Outputs:  
	Utility creates variables TRTA, TRTP, APERIOD, APERIODC, APHASE, 
        APERDY, APERSDY, APEREDY, APERSDT, APEREDT, APERSTM, APERETM, 
        APERSDTM and APEREDTM variables. APERDY, APERSDY and APEREDY variables
        will be created for only crossover study. APERSDY and APEREDY variables 
        will be created only if start and end dates are passed in the respective
        parameters.

References: 
        Refer to docs in Data Standards Code
        <gen_tp_join_adsl Programming Spec>

Parameters : 
        _dsnin - Name of the input dataset             
        _dsnout - Name of the output dataset           
        _trtoption - Option to use or not use gap in between the analysis periods to 
                     derive TRTA, TRTAN, TRTP and TRTPN variables. 
                     Valid values are OPTION1 and OPTION2
                     OPTION1 - Does not consider the gap between previous analysis 
                               period end date and current analysis period start date
                               in calculating TRTA, TRTAN, TRTP and TRTPN variables.
                     OPTION2 - Considers the gap between previous analysis period 
                               end date and current analysis period start date
                               in calculating TRTA, TRTAN, TRTP and TRTPN variables.          
         _dropvars - Variables to drop from the output dataset. 
         _analstartdtvar - If an endpoint has both start date and end date then 
                           analysis start date will be passed. If an endpoint has 
                           only analysis date then the analysis date variable will 
                           be passed.
         _analstarttmvar - If an endpoint has both start time and end time then 
                           analysis start time will be passed. If an endpoint has 
                           only analysis time then the analysis time variable will 
                           be passed. If time is not collected, the parameter is
                           set to missing.
         _analstartdtmvar - If an endpoint has start date-time (or) analysis date-time 
                            variable already created in the input dataset, it can be 
                            passed in this parameter. If set to missing and time 
                            variable is passed in _analstarttmvar, then a temporary
                            date-time variable will be created for analysis using
                            the variables passed in _analstartdtvar and
                            _analstarttmvar parameters  
         _analenddtvar - If an endpoint has both start date and end date then 
                         analysis end date will be passed. If an endpoint has 
                         only analysis date then the parameter is set to 
                         missing.
         _analendtmvar - If an endpoint has both start time and end time then 
                         analysis end time will be passed. If an endpoint has 
                         only analysis time or if time is not collected, 
                         the parameter is set to missing.
         _analenddtmvar - If an endpoint has end datetime (or) analysis end datetime 
                          variable already created in the input dataset, it can be 
                          passed in this parameter. If set to missing and time 
                          variable is passed in _analendtmvar, then a temporary
                          datetime variable will be created for analysis using
                          the variables passed in _analenddtvar and
                          _analendtmvar parameters  

        G_ADSL_PRE_LAG parameter is used to define the number of minutes to adjust to the
        start of each period. It is defined in ad<xx>.txt file. Default is 0 minutes.
 
Usage notes:

The calculations for TRTA TRTP TRTAN TRTPN APHASE APERIOD APERIODC APERSDT APEREDT 
APERSTM APERETM APERSDTM APEREDTM below are based on assumption that ADT is the 
analysis variable. If user passes ASTDT/AENDT then ADT should be replaced with 
ASTDT in the calculations below:
 
TRTA TRTP TRTAN TRTPN APERIOD and APERIODC Calculation: User has two options to calculate 
these variables. The option will be passed using the parameter _trtoption:

  OPTION1: Does not consider the gap in between analysis periods in determining 
           TRTA TRTP TRTAN TRTPN APERIOD APERIODC variables.
    If AP[xx]SDT <= ADT <= AP[xx]EDT then: TRTP = TRT[xx]P, TRTPN = TRT[xx]PN,
                                           TRTA = TRT[xx]A, TRTAN = TRT[xx]AN,
                                           APERIOD = [xx] (ex: 1,2,3, etc),
                                           APERIODC = "Period [xx]" (ex: Period 01, Period 02, etc)
 
    If time is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date-time values. 
    If only date is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date values.
    [xx] has value of 1 to (number of periods) incremented by 1

  OPTION2: This considers the gap in between analysis periods, before first period 
           start date and last period end date in determining TRTA TRTP TRTAN 
           TRTPN variables.
    For Period 1: 
        If ADT <= AP01EDT: TRTP = TRT01P, TRTPN = TRT01PN, TRTA = TRT01A, 
                           TRTAN = TRT01AN, APERIOD = 1, APERIODC = "Period 01",
    For Period 2 until last before period:
        Else If AP[xx-1]EDT < ADT <= AP[xx]EDT: TRTP = TRT[xx]P, TRTPN = TRT[xx]PN, 
                                                TRTA = TRT[xx]A, TRTAN = TRT[xx]AN,
                                                APERIOD = [xx] (ex: 2,3, etc),
                                                APERIODC = "Period [xx]" (ex: Period 02, etc)
        where [xx] has value of 2 to (number of periods - 1) incremented by 1. 
              [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.
    For the last period:
        Else if ADT > AP[xx-1]EDT: TRTP = TRT[xx]P, TRTPN = TRT[xx]PN, TRTA = TRT[xx]A, 
                                   TRTAN = TRT[xx]AN, APERIOD = [xx] (ex: 2,3, etc),
                                   APERIODC = "Period [xx]" (ex: Period 02, etc)
        where [xx] is the last period. 
              [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.
  If time is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date-time values. 
  If only date is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date values.

APHASE Calculation:
  For [xx] = 01
    If ADT <= AP[xx]SDT: APHASE = "PRE-TREATMENT"
    else If AP[xx]SDT < ADT <= AP[xx]EDT: APHASE = "TREATMENT [xx]"
    If there is only 1 period then, if ADT > AP[xx]EDT: APHASE = "FOLLOW-UP"
  For [xx] = 2 to (number of periods - 1) incremented by 1
    If AP[xx-1]EDT < ADT <= AP[xx]SDT: APHASE = "OFFDRUG [xx-1]"
    If AP[xx]SDT < ADT <= AP[xx]EDT: APHASE = "TREATMENT [xx]"
       where [xx] has value of 2 to (number of periods - 1) incremented by 1. 
             [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.
  For [xx] having the value of last period
    If AP[xx-1]EDT < ADT <= AP[xx]SDT: APHASE = "OFFDRUG [xx-1]"
    Else If AP[xx]SDT < ADT <= AP[xx]EDT: APHASE = "TREATMENT [xx]"
    Else if ADT > AP[xx]EDT: APHASE = "FOLLOW-UP"
       where [xx] is the last period. 
             [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.
  If time is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date-time values. 
  If only date is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date values.

APERDY Calculation (only for endpoints with Analysis date and not start and end dates):
  Analysis date variable is passed in _analstartdtvar parameter and Analysis time if
  present is populated in  _analstarttmvar parameter.

  For period 1 - Period subset condition: ADTM <= AP01EDTM
    If ADT < AP01SDT then APERDY = ADT - AP01SDT
    Else if ADT >= AP01SDT then APERDY = ADT - AP01SDT + 1
    AP01SDT, ADT will be date values. AP01EDTM and ADTM
    will be date-time values.

  For periods other than last period - 
    Period subset condition: AP[xx-1]EDTM < ADTM <=AP[xx]EDTM
    If ADT < AP[xx]SDT then APERDY = ADT - AP[xx]SDT
    Else if ADT >= AP[xx]SDT then APERDY = ADT - AP[xx]SDT + 1
    where xx has value of 2 to (number of periods - 1) incremented by 1
    AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date values and AP[xx]SDTM, AP[xx]EDTM, ADTM
    will be date-time values. [xx-1] is the period before [xx].

  For last period - Period subset condition: ADTM > AP[xx-1]EDTM
    If ADT < AP[xx]SDT then APERDY = ADT - AP[xx]SDT
    Else if ADT >= AP[xx]SDT then APERDY = ADT - AP[xx]SDT + 1
       where [xx] is the last period. 
             [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.    
    AP[xx]SDT and ADT will be date values and AP[xx-1]EDTM, ADTM
    will be date-time values. [xx-1] is the period before [xx].
APERSDY Calculation (For endpoints with Analysis start and end dates):
  Analysis start date variable is passed in _analstartdtvar parameter. 

  For period 1 - Period subset condition: ASTDTM <= AP01EDTM
    If ASTDT < AP01SDT then APERSDY = ASTDT - AP01SDT
    Else if ASTDT >= AP01SDT then APERSDY = ASTDT - AP01SDT + 1
    AP01SDT, ASTDT will be date values. AP01EDTM and ASTDTM
    will be date-time values.

  For periods other than last period - 
  Period subset condition: AP[xx-1]EDTM < ASTDTM <=AP[xx]EDTM
    If ASTDT < AP[xx]SDT then APERSDY = ASTDT - AP[xx]SDT
    Else if ASTDT >= AP[xx]SDT then APERSDY = ASTDT - AP[xx]SDT + 1
    where xx has value of 2 to (number of periods - 1) incremented by 1
    AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ASTDT will be date values and AP[xx]SDTM, AP[xx]EDTM 
    and ASTDTM will be date-time values. [xx-1] is the period before [xx].

  For last period - Period subset condition: ASTDTM > AP[xx-1]EDTM
    If ASTDT < AP[xx]SDT then APERSDY = ASTDT - AP[xx]SDT
    Else if ADT >= AP[xx]SDT then APERSDY = ASTDT - AP[xx]SDT + 1
       where [xx] is the last period. 
             [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.    
    AP[xx]SDT and ASTDT will be date values and AP[xx-1]EDTM, ASTDTM
    will be date-time values. [xx-1] is the period before [xx].
APEREDY Calculation (For endpoints with Analysis start and end dates):
  Analysis end date variable is passed in _analenddtvar parameter.

  For period 1 - Period subset condition: AENDTM <= AP01EDTM
    If AENDT < AP01SDT then APEREDY = AENDT - AP01SDT
    Else if AENDT >= AP01SDT then APEREDY = AENDT - AP01SDT + 1
    AP01SDT, AENDT will be date values. AP01EDTM and AENDTM
    will be date-time values.

  For other periods- Period subset condtion: AP[xx-1]EDT < AENDT <=AP[xx]EDT
    If AENDT < AP[xx]SDT then APEREDY = AENDT - AP[xx]SDT
    Else if AENDT >= AP[xx]SDT then APEREDY = AENDT - AP[xx]SDT + 1
    where xx has value of 2 to (number of periods - 1) incremented by 1
    AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, AENDT will be date values and AP[xx]SDTM, AP[xx]EDTM 
    and AENDTM will be date-time values. [xx-1] is the period before [xx].
 
  For last period - Period subset condition: ASTDTM > AP[xx-1]EDTM
    If AENDT < AP[xx]SDT then APEREDY = AENDT - AP[xx]SDT
    Else if AENDT >= AP[xx]SDT then APEREDY = AENDT - AP[xx]SDT + 1
       where [xx] is the last period. 
             [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.    
    AP[xx]SDT and AENDT will be date values and AP[xx-1]EDTM, AENDTM
    will be date-time values. [xx-1] is the period before [xx].
APERSDT APEREDT APERSTM APERETM APERSDTM and APEREDTM calculation:
  For Period 1: 
      If ADT <= AP01EDT: APERSDT = AP01SDT, APERSTM = AP01STM, APEREDT = AP01EDT
                         APERETM = AP01ETM, APERSDTM = AP01SDTM, APEREDTM = AP01EDTM 
  For Period 2 until last before period:
      Else If AP[xx-1]EDT < ADT <= AP[xx]EDT: APERSDT = AP[xx]SDT, APEREDT = AP[xx]EDT,  
                                              APERSTM = AP[xx]STM, APERETM = AP[xx]ETM, 
                                              APERSDTM = AP[xx]SDTM, APEREDTM = AP[xx]EDTM
      where [xx] has value of 2 to (number of periods - 1) incremented by 1. 
            [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.
  APERSTM, APERETM, APERSDTM and APEREDTM will only be collected when time 
  is captured.
  For the last period:
      Else if ADT > AP[xx-1]EDT: APERSDT = AP[xx]SDT, APEREDT = AP[xx]EDT,  
                                 APERSTM = AP[xx]STM, APERETM = AP[xx]ETM, 
                                 APERSDTM = AP[xx]SDTM, APEREDTM = AP[xx]EDTM 
      where [xx] is the last period. 
            [xx-1] is the period before [xx]. Ex: If [xx] = 02 then [xx-1] = 01.
  If time is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date-time values. 
  If only date is collected then AP[xx]SDT, AP[xx]EDT, ADT will be date values.
  APERSTM, APERETM, APERSDTM and APEREDTM will only be created when time 
  is captured.

Examples:

%gen_tp_join_adsl(_dsnin = _dsnin
                  ,_dsnout = _dsnin
                  ,_trtoption = OPTION1
                  ,_dropvars =
                  ,_analstartdtvar=ADT
                  ,_analstarttmvar=ATM
                  ,_analstartdtmvar=ADTM
                  ,_analenddtvar=
                  ,_analendtmvar=
                  ,_analenddtmvar=
                  );
  The above example creates TRTA TRTP TRTAN TRTPN APERIOD APERIODC APERSDY APEREDY APHASE APERDY
  APERSDT APERSTM APEREDT APERETM APERSDTM and APEREDTM variables for a crossover study.

%gen_tp_join_adsl(_dsnin = _dsnin
                  ,_dsnout = _dsnin
                  ,_trtoption = OPTION2
                  ,_dropvars = APERSDY APEREDY
                  ,_analstartdtvar=ASTDT
                  ,_analstarttmvar=
                  ,_analstartdtmvar=
                  ,_analenddtvar= AENDT
                  ,_analendtmvar= 
                  ,_analenddtmvar=
                  );
  The above example creates TRTA TRTP TRTAN TRTPN APERIOD APERIODC APHASE APERSDT and APEREDT 
  variables for a crossover study.
           
